-- title:
--   Genus does not drop under algebraically closed constant field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq K' \subseteq F'$ and $K \subseteq F \subseteq F'$ be fields with compatible algebra structures (two scalar towers $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$), with $K$ and $K'$ algebraically closed. Assume that $F$ is a one-variable function field over $K$ in the explicit sense that there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over $K(x)$, and likewise that there is $x' \in F'$ transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite-dimensional over $K'(x')$. Assume further `IsCurveOver K F` and `IsCurveOver K' F'`, i.e. for each of the two extensions: every nonzero $f$ admits a divisor $D$ with $D(v) = v(\operatorname{ord} f)$ at all places $v$ and $\deg D = 0$ (places being valuation subrings of the function field that contain the constants, are not the whole field, and are principal ideal rings), every place has residue field finite-dimensional over the constant field, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one over the function field. Finally assume $F'$ is generated as a field over $K'$ by the image of $F$, i.e. the $K'$-subfield of $F'$ generated by $\operatorname{range}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ F\ F')$ is $\top$. Then $\mathrm{genusFF}\ K\ F \le \mathrm{genusFF}\ K'\ F'$, where $\mathrm{genusFF}$ of a function field is the $K$-dimension of the adelic $H^1$ of the zero divisor.
--
--   This is one inequality of the classical invariance of the genus under extension of an algebraically closed constant field; it is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.genusFF_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed), which combines it with the reverse inequality to identify the two genera.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_le_genusFF_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve

theorem AlgebraicCurve.le_genusFF_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed (K F K' F' : Type*)
    [Field K] [Field F] [Field K'] [Field F'] [Algebra K F] [Algebra K' F']
    [Algebra K K'] [Algebra F F'] [Algebra K F'] [IsScalarTower K K' F'] [IsScalarTower K F F']
    [IsAlgClosed K] [IsAlgClosed K']
    (hfg : ∃ x : F, Transcendental K x ∧ FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F)
    (hfg' : ∃ x : F', Transcendental K' x ∧
      FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K' ({x} : Set F')) F')
    [IsCurveOver K F] [IsCurveOver K' F']
    (hgen : IntermediateField.adjoin K' (Set.range (algebraMap F F')) = ⊤) :
    genusFF K F ≤ genusFF K' F' := by sorry
